{"name":"Maiden Voyage","hex":"#8ac7d4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maiden voyage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The first trip of a vessel in its intended duty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden_voyage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maiden Voyage (Herbie Hancock album)","blocks":[{"text":"Maiden Voyage is the fifth album led by jazz musician Herbie Hancock, and was recorded by Rudy Van Gelder on March 17, 1965, for Blue Note Records. It was issued as BLP 4195 and BST 84195. Featuring Hancock with tenor saxophonist George Coleman, trumpeter Freddie Hubbard, bassist Ron Carter and drummer Tony Williams, it is a concept album aimed at creating an oceanic atmosphere. As such, many of the track titles refer to marine biology or the sea, and the musicians develop the concept through their use of space. The album was presented with the Grammy Hall of Fame Award in 1999."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/Maiden_Voyage_%28Hancock%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maiden_Voyage_(Herbie_Hancock_album)","wikidata":"Q908746"},{"title":"Maiden Voyage (composition)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Maiden Voyage\" is a jazz composition by Herbie Hancock from his 1965 album Maiden Voyage. It features Hancock's quartet – trumpeter Freddie Hubbard, bassist Ron Carter and drummer Tony Williams – together with saxophonist George Coleman. It is one of Hancock's best-known compositions and has become a jazz standard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Maiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png/330px-Maiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maiden_Voyage_(composition)","wikidata":"Q6735404"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7a/Maiden_Voyage_%28Hancock%29.jpg/250px-Maiden_Voyage_%28Hancock%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/Maiden_Voyage_%28Hancock%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7a/Maiden_Voyage_%28Hancock%29.jpg/250px-Maiden_Voyage_%28Hancock%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaiden_Voyage_(Hancock).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Maiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png/330px-Maiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Maiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png/330px-Maiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Maiden Voyage\" opening vamp: Dsus chord in D Dorian,[1] or mixolydian.[2] Playⓘ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaiden_Voyage_Herbie_Hancock_opening_vamp.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Minor_eleventh_chord_Herbie_Hancock_Maiden_Voyage.png/500px-Minor_eleventh_chord_Herbie_Hancock_Maiden_Voyage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Minor_eleventh_chord_Herbie_Hancock_Maiden_Voyage.png/500px-Minor_eleventh_chord_Herbie_Hancock_Maiden_Voyage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Opening chord: minor eleventh chord (Am9/D).[6] Playⓘ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinor_eleventh_chord_Herbie_Hancock_Maiden_Voyage.png"}],"sounds":{}}}